Set up a Next.js project.

Install Axios or another HTTP client.

Create API service files (e.g., api/articles.js).

Implement login form and POST to /login.

Store auth token (Sanctum or Bearer) in cookies or local storage.

Set up global auth state (e.g., using Context API or Zustand).

Fetch public data: articles, categories, tags, pages, settings, files.

Display article list and detail pages.

Create category, tag, page, and file browsing components.

Create authenticated layout/pages.

Add profile settings: get user, update user, change password, logout.

Build article, page, category, tag, file CRUD (admin only).

Use route protection for authenticated pages.

Implement UI feedback (loading, error, success messages).

Deploy backend and frontend with environment variables set.